      "id": "inputs.degree-two.statement",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "A uniform degree-two estimate",
      "anchor": "inputs-degree-two",
      "statement": "One C works for every prime ℓ, every totally complex number field L containing a primitive root of order ℓ (4 at ℓ=2), every algebraic closure and compatible choices of local places and characters, and every natural e≥1. H²(G_S,ℤ_ℓ(e+1)) is finite and its logarithmic order is ≤ exp((2e[L:ℚ])^C log(2|disc L|)).",
      "hypotheses": "S is the full set of finite primes over ℓ. The compatible character descends the cyclotomic character to the unramified-outside-S quotient. The proof uses the rank bound on selected stabilized odd-degree classes, Poitou–Tate duality, local finiteness and local Tate duality.",
      "definitions": [
        "finite length",
        "absolute discriminant",
        "cyclotomic twist",
        "primitive fourth root at ℓ=2"
      ],
      "dependencies": [
        "inputs.degree-two.local"
      ],
      "correspondence": "WindowBoundOfLiteratureLevel obtains the witness from lemmaK_litN_alt; KFinal supplies bOdd and lemmaK_of_litN_alt passes the three cohomological hypotheses to the ClassCounting proof. The window applies the result at its exceptional layer.",
