      "id": "inputs.degree-two.layer",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "Cyclotomic enlargement and its discriminant cost",
      "anchor": "inputs-degree-two-layer",
      "statement": "There is an auxiliary totally complex cyclotomic layer of degree d≤(n+1)(4e+4), with n′=dn and maximal root depth c. Both r₂(L′) and ℓ^c exceed 2e+1; ℓ^c≤2n′, Δ′≤Δ^d(ℓ^c)^n′, and the locally trivial length over L is at most its value over L′.",
      "hypotheses": "Root and positive twist assumptions of the degree-two bound. Monotonicity uses the tower descent description of the locally trivial group.",
      "definitions": [
        "local conditions on decomposition and inertia",
        "relative different",
        "maximal depth of roots of unity"
      ],
      "dependencies": [
        "FCT-02"
      ],
      "correspondence": "The relative degree is ℓ^m, m the least exponent reaching 4e+4. Differentiating a cyclotomic relation gives divisibility of the norm of the different; factorization of g^{ℓ^m}−1 gives the quotient surjection on the descent side.",
