      "statement": "In the auxiliary field, for all eligible depths ν, the number of class characters satisfying φ(γ⁻¹P)=aφ(P) is bounded by T_(2e) T_(2e+1) ℓ^X with a=(1+ℓ^c)^e, X=(b+vℓ(e))g+c+vℓ(e). The same bound holds for ℓ raised to the local-triviality length.",
      "hypotheses": "The auxiliary field has r₂,ℓ^c>2e+1 and c≥2 when ℓ=2. The cycle construction, local-to-global power detection, primitive evaluation bound and the Selmer comparison are used.",
